  "notes": "Substitutions from the four-engine granite-4.1-3b run, each engine-level and disclosed. Measured on the Windows/WSL2 box: RTX 3070 (sm_86 Ampere, 8 GB, driver 596.36); SGLang 0.5.17 / torch 2.11.0+cu130 / flashinfer 0.6.15 / xgrammar 0.2.1. (1) MODEL - granite-4.1-3b is an internal IBM checkpoint whose safetensors were not obtainable on this box, so Qwen3-1.7B (Qwen3ForCausalLM, tool-call-parser qwen) was served - the same substitute model the TensorRT-LLM column used. The truncation property is an engine guarantee, not model quality, so this measures SGLang behaviour, not a quality cross-compare. (2) enable_thinking=false - Qwen3 is a reasoning model; with thinking on it spends the whole budget in <think> and never reaches the JSON even at 64 (the control would fail), so thinking is disabled via chat_template_kwargs to make it a direct tool-caller comparable to the non-reasoning granite the other engines served. (3) tool_choice - unlike TensorRT-LLM 1.2.1, SGLang ACCEPTS tool_choice:required (HTTP 200), matching the granite/vLLM/runner columns; this report is the required run. tool_choice:auto was also measured and yields byte-identical per-rung verdicts. Guided-decoding backend xgrammar; attention-backend triton with --disable-cuda-graph (CUDA-graph capture needs nvcc/CUDA_HOME on this fresh box and is irrelevant to the tool-call verdict).",
